<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="c1f21b04">&lt;p&gt;
    If benefits tracking shows that benefits are not being realized to the extent to which they were expected, the
    program/project should undertake an action planning task. This task may be initiated centrally, however, it is likely
    that it will need involvement of those close to the&amp;nbsp;business unit&amp;nbsp;being impacted by the change.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    One of the reasons for tracking benefits&amp;nbsp;is to drive action. This&amp;nbsp;task is focused on the development of
    action plans where actual performance is significantly different&amp;nbsp;when compared to&amp;nbsp;expected performance.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Consideration should be given to incorporating key tasks from the action plans into the program/project plan. In some
    cases business case and benefits realization plan might need an update. These updates should be carefully tracked.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="b989424c"></attribute>
