<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="c3610e0a">An action plan should be prepared for the underperforming benefits. Ideally, this should be completed by the benefit owner.
If this is not possible, the&amp;nbsp;program/project team should facilitate the completion of the action plans&amp;nbsp;through
engagement with key stakeholders. The completed action plans should be reviewed with the program sponsor and the benefit
owner.&amp;nbsp;The purpose of the action plan should be to identify appropriate remedial actions in order to improve benefit
performance and get it to an acceptable level. This could be achieved by modifying process steps, issuing targeted
communications, and editing training module materials.</attribute>
